// What `#![repository(E)]` says when nothing provides the three names its generated functions
// call. **One error naming all three**, where this used to be nine "use of undefined variable
// 'note_meta'" errors -- one per generated function that mentioned it, each pointing at the module
// attribute and naming a symbol the author never wrote.
//
// The message names the derives that write them *and* says they may be written by hand, because
// the check is by name: `tests/lang/repository_handwritten_meta` is a repository over three
// hand-written definitions and no derives at all.
#![repository(Note)]

use datasource
use db.DbError

struct Note {
    #[pk]
    id: int
    body: string
}

fn main() {
    print("x")
}
